# The token-fixture generator creates a throwaway RSA key on every run and drops it
# next to the corpus. No key is ever committed -- that is why the fixtures can be.
signing-key.pem

# The second admitted caller, written only by an in-place regeneration. The live
# corpus `--out` writes is where it is read from; a copy here is a leftover, and
# an untracked one is a file `provision.sh` would copy into the CI tree.
positive_other_user.jwt
